Z||000008||Oreif||08-01-2000||11:08 AM||||There are 2 cruise nights related to the club on August 10. One is in Crystal Lake the other is in Joliet. There is also a cruise night in Elmhurst on Aug 9th.<P>The Joliet one is at Chicago Street and Van Buren across from thr Rialto Theater. <P>The Crystal Lake one is on Willams Street just south of Woodstock Street. <P>The Elmhurst one is York Road between St. Charles Road and North Ave. Parking starts at Robert Palmer road and goes north.<BR>(suppose to be one of the larger Cruise nights) <P>On August 3rd there is one in Glen Ellyn for "Custom and Modified Cars". It's on Main Street just north of the railroad tracks.<P>All of them are 7pm to 9pm.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||08-01-2000||11:26 AM||||For the Car Shows, <BR>There is the Orphan Auto Picnic on Sunday 20 August 1020 Aurora Avenue Aurora ILL 11am to 5pm (no judging, no admission fee) (Jim and Paul will be here)<P>On 26th August is the Central Ill show in El Paso ILL<P>On 27 August the All Pontiac Show With great Trophy's. It's at McDonald's 2111 Midwest Road in Oak Brook, IL registration is 8am to 11am Show is 11am until 4pm. I am pre-registered for this show already.<P>On 10 September is our clubs Fierorama. Same place as the All Pontiac show listed above 11am to 5pm. I am also pre-registered for this one. There are no prizes for mine or your car. They only give prizes to "daily Drivers with 3 mods or less" Actually you may get in since so far it's just suspension and wheels. They also give special awards for "Hard Luck", "Highest Mileage" (for each year), "Most Damage" (must be driven in not towed) and Ronald McDonald's choice.<P>If I hear of any more I'll let you know.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
